# Paths Semgrep must not scan.
#
# Read automatically by every `semgrep scan`, so it applies to the registry packs in
# `.github/workflows/semgrep.yml` as well as to `.semgrep/rules/`. Keeping the list here rather
# than in CLI flags means a local run and a CI run see the same repository.

# Build output and dependencies.
node_modules/
mobile/node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.expo/
ios/Pods/
android/

# Vendored third-party agent skills — installed by `npx skills add`, not authored here.
# Measured 2026-08-08: 43 of 45 findings on the first full run came from this one directory,
# almost all of them `innerHTML` inside `skills/impeccable/scripts/live-browser.js`, a bundled
# browser-automation harness. Scanning code we do not maintain produces findings nobody can act
# on, which is the fastest way to teach a team to ignore a scanner. `.claude/skills/VENDORED-EXTERNAL.md`
# draws the same line for the same reason.
skills/

# The Claude Design export. One HTML file of base64-gzipped assets; there is no source to review.
design/

# Semgrep's own fixture. `.semgrep/rules/xoot.tsx` exists to make every rule fire, so scanning it
# would report six findings by design. `semgrep --test` passes the file explicitly and is not
# affected by this list.
.semgrep/

